<h1>Current iPhone Lineup</h1>
<p>
  The iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max lead the lineup with the A20 Pro, whose three-tier CPU pairs 2 super cores with 4 efficiency cores alongside a 7-core GPU with Neural Accelerators and a dual 16-core Neural Engine. The Pro pairs it with Apple's second-generation C2 modem; the Pro Max does not. The iPhone Duo, Apple's first foldable, uses the same A20 Pro and C2 combination.
  The iPhone 17 Pro and Pro Max carry the A19 Pro with a 6-core GPU, and the iPhone Air the same chip with 5 GPU cores. The iPhone 17 uses the standard A19, which shares the CPU but has a lower GPU configuration and no ProRes hardware, and the iPhone 17e carries the A19 with fewer GPU cores again for a lower price point. The iPhone 16 and 16 Plus remain on sale with the A18 — still powerful, but two generations behind on Neural Engine performance and efficiency.
</p>

